# This is a sample file distributed with Galaxy that is used to define
# HuggingFace pre-trained models for the "Protein Language Modelling" tool,
# using 7 tab-separated columns.
# Lines starting with "#" are ignored by Galaxy.
#
# This tool reuses the shared "huggingface" data table (also consumed by the
# tabicl and RAG Retriever tools). Each tool family selects its own rows via
# the free_tag column, so protein language models do not collide with models
# registered for other tools.
#
# Columns (TAB-separated):
#   value	name	pipeline_tag	domain	free_tag	version	path
#
#   value         Unique row ID across the whole huggingface.loc table
#   name          Human-readable label shown in the Galaxy select widget
#   pipeline_tag  Official HuggingFace pipeline tag; all three model families
#                 below use "feature-extraction"
#                 (https://huggingface.co/models?pipeline_tag=feature-extraction)
#   domain        Coarse model family; use "protein" for all rows below
#   free_tag      Per-tool-family namespace used as the primary XML filter;
#                 Protein Language Modelling rows use "protein-lm"
#   version       Tool version these rows belong to; used as a secondary XML filter
#   path          Path to the local model folder on this server. The folder
#                 must contain config.json, tokenizer files, and safetensors
#                 weights (see the tool's help text -- pytorch_model.bin
#                 checkpoints are rejected for security reasons)
#
# Administrators: copy this file to your Galaxy tool-data directory as
# "huggingface.loc" and update each path to point to the actual model
# directory on this server. The model's family (ESM-2 / ProtBERT / ProtT5) is
# detected at runtime from that directory's config.json, never from the path
# or name here, so any Hugging Face checkpoint of one of these three
# architectures can be registered.
#
# For the full shared schema reference see:
#   https://galaxyproject.org/news/2026-04-13-huggingface-data-table/
#
# Example entries (replace each path with the real location on your server):
#
# facebook/esm2_t33_650M_UR50D	ESM-2 650M (esm2_t33_650M_UR50D)	feature-extraction	protein	protein-lm	1	/data/models/esm2_t33_650M_UR50D
# Rostlab/prot_bert	ProtBERT	feature-extraction	protein	protein-lm	1	/data/models/prot_bert
# Rostlab/prot_t5_xl_half_uniref50-enc	ProtT5-XL half-precision encoder	feature-extraction	protein	protein-lm	1	/data/models/prot_t5_xl_half_uniref50-enc
